$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 3. To a solution of
triphenylphosphine oxide (42 mg, 0.15 mmol) in either CHCl3 or CDCl3 (1.5
mL) were added oxalyl chloride (16.5 μL, 0.195mmol) and LiBr (130-304mg,
1.50-3.50 mmol), and the reaction mixture stirred for 5 min. The
appropriate alcohol (1.00 equiv) and oxalyl chloride (93.5 μL, 1.11 mmol)
as solutions in either CHCl3 or CDCl3 (1.0 mL) were then added
simultaneously over 5 h via syringe pump at rt. The reaction mixture was
filtered. The solvent was removed in vacuo. Further purification by flash
chromatography (silica, 5-10% Et2O/petroleum ether) gave the pure
bromides. 1-Bromomethylbenzene (11b) as a colorless oil, yield 121 mg,
71%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.45-7.30 (m, 5H, ArH), 4.52 (s, 2H, CH2);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 137.9, 129.1, 128.9, 128.5, 33.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Appel reaction, slow simultaneous addition of alcohol and oxalyl chloride
stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic Phosphorus(V)-Mediated Nucleophilic Substitution Reactions:
Development of a Catalytic Appel Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Denton, Ross M.; An, Jie; Adeniran, Beatrice; Blake, Alexander J.; Lewis,
William; Poulton, Andrew M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2011), 76(16), 6749-6767

