$DATUM Benzyl Chlorides 4 from Alcohols 3; General Procedure B: Ph3P (3 equiv)
and CH2Cl2 (2 mL per 3.0 mmol Ph3P) were added to a flask equipped with a
magnetic stir bar. CBrCl3 (1.2 equiv) was added, the flask was closed
with a septum, and the mixture was stirred under air at r.t. for 40 min,
during which the colorless soln turned deep brown. A soln of the
requisite alcohol 3 (1.0 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (3 mL per 1.0 mmol alcohol) was
added dropwise, and the mixture was stirred at r.t. until the starting
material had been consumed (as indicated by TLC; approximately 10 min).
The mixture was diluted with a Et2O-pentane mixture (3:1) until solid
Ph3PO began to precipitate. The heterogeneous mixture was then filtered
through a pad of silica gel, which was rinsed with a Et2O-pentane mixture
(3:1). Rotary evaporation provided clean 4 after most reactions, as
indicated by 1H NMR spectroscopy. The products were purified additionally
by flash chromatography. The product was purified by flash column
chromatography (silica gel, pentane); this provided 4a.
1-(Chloromethyl)-2-iodobenzene (4a) as a colorless oil, yield 238 mg,
94%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.86 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1 H), 7.48 (d, J =
7.7 Hz, 1 H), 7.37 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.01 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 1 H), 4.67
(s, 2 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 139.9 (2C), 130.2, 130.1, 128.8,
99.5, 51.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Appel reaction, alternative reaction conditions shown, alternative
reaction conditions gave lower yield
