$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (4R,5R)-5-[(Chloro-diphenyl)methyl]-2,2-dimethyl-α,α-diphenyl-1,3-dioxolane-4-methanol
(2). Triphenylphosphine (4.5 g, 17.0 mmol) and TADDOL 1 (4.0 g, 8.6 mmol)
were dissolved in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (15 mL) under argon atmosphere.
Pyridine (1.4 mL, 17.0 mmol) and CCl4 (1.7 mL, 17.0 mmol) were added and
the reaction mixture was stirred for 3 d at rt. After concentration to a
volume of ca. 5 mL the solution was flash chromatographed (silica gel
(250 g), pentane/Et2O 4:1) and the obtained product recrystallized
(pentane/Et2O 6:1 (20 mL)). 2 (3.0 g, 72%) as a white solid. Rf 0.58
(pentane/Et2O 4:1); mp 133-135 °C; [α]D rt =-17.8 (c = 1.45, CHCl3); 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.91 (s, CH3); 1.07 (s, CH3); 1.82 (s, OH); 5.12
(d, J = 5.9 Hz, CH); 5.36 (d, J = 5.9 Hz, CH); 7.15-7.42 (m, 18 arom. H);
7.47-7.51 (m, 2 arom. H). All analytical data were in accordance with the
literature values.1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM key intermediate, Appel reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of TADDOL Derivatives for New Applications
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Seebach, Dieter; Pichota, Arkadius; Beck, Albert K.; Pinkerton, Anthony
B.; Litz, Thomas; Karjalainen, Jaana; Gramlich, Volker
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (1999), 1(1), 55-58

