or CDCl3 (1.5 mL) was added oxalyl chloride (15.0 μL, 0.177 mmol), and
the reaction mixture was stirred for 5 min. The appropriate alcoho (1.00
equiv) and oxalyl chloride (87.0 μL, 1.03 mmol) as solutions in either
CHCl3 or CDCl3 (1.0 mL) were then added simultaneously over 7 h via
syringe pump at rt. The solvent was removed in vacuo. Purification by
flash chromatography (silica, 5-100% Et2O/petroleum ether) gave the pure
chlorides. 1-Chloro-2-butene (8g), yield 64 mg, 70%. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 5.80 (m, 1H, H3CCHCHCH2Cl), 5.64 (m, 1H, H3CCHCHCH2Cl), 4.02
(dt, J = 7.0 and 0.9 Hz, 2H, CH2Cl), 1.73 (m, 3H, CH3); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 130.1, 129.1, 45.4, 17.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Appel reaction, slow simultaneous addition of alcohol and oxalyl chloride
stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic Phosphorus(V)-Mediated Nucleophilic Substitution Reactions:
Development of a Catalytic Appel Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
